{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "text": "What is a dictionary?",
      "options": [
        "Pairs of key: value, where we look a value up by its key",
        "A list whose elements are kept sorted",
        "A variable that holds exactly one name",
        "A list of values we read by their position"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "text": "Which brackets make a dictionary?",
      "options": ["[ ]", "{ }", "( )", "< >"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "text": "In `{\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\"}`, what is `\"Cortez\"`?",
      "options": ["The value", "The index", "The key", "The dictionary's name"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "phone_book = {\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\", \"Lance\": \"555-5678\"}\nprint(phone_book[\"Sonny\"])",
      "options": [
        "It prints nothing",
        "It prints Sonny",
        "It prints the last number, 555-5678",
        "It stops with a KeyError: there is no key Sonny"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "text": "phone_book has no key \"Tommy\". What does `phone_book[\"Tommy\"] = \"555-0000\"` do?",
      "options": [
        "It adds Tommy with that number",
        "It stops with a KeyError",
        "It changes the first number in phone_book",
        "Nothing, Tommy has to be added with append"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "text": "phone_book already has Lance. What does `phone_book[\"Lance\"] = \"555-1111\"` do?",
      "options": [
        "It adds a second Lance, so the old number stays too",
        "It replaces Lance's number: a key is in a dictionary only once",
        "It stops with an error: Lance is already there",
        "It does nothing, the old number stays"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "text": "Which line removes Lance from phone_book?",
      "options": [
        "phone_book[\"Lance\"] = \"\"",
        "phone_book.append(\"Lance\")",
        "del phone_book[\"Lance\"]",
        "del \"Lance\""
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "text": "How do we check that phone_book has the key Cortez before we read it?",
      "options": [
        "if phone_book[\"Cortez\"]:",
        "if phone_book == \"Cortez\":",
        "if \"Cortez\" = phone_book:",
        "if \"Cortez\" in phone_book:"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "phone_book = {\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\"}\nprint(\"555-1234\" in phone_book)",
      "options": [
        "False: in looks at the keys, and 555-1234 is a value",
        "True: 555-1234 is in the dictionary",
        "Cortez",
        "It stops with a KeyError"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q10",
      "text": "When is a dictionary a better choice than a list?",
      "options": [
        "When the values have to stay sorted",
        "When we look values up by a name, not by their position",
        "When we have only numbers",
        "When the values must never change"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q11",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "scores = {\"Cortez\": 1, \"Lance\": 2, \"Phil\": 3}\nscores[\"Lance\"] = 5\nprint(scores)",
      "options": [
        "{'Cortez': 1, 'Phil': 3, 'Lance': 5}",
        "{'Cortez': 1, 'Lance': 2, 'Phil': 3, 'Lance': 5}",
        "{'Cortez': 1, 'Lance': 5, 'Phil': 3}",
        "It stops with an error: Lance is already there"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q12",
      "text": "What can the values of a dictionary be?",
      "options": [
        "Only text",
        "Only numbers",
        "Only text and numbers",
        "Any kind of value: text, numbers, booleans, even lists or other dictionaries"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q13",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "phone_book = {\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\"}\nprint(phone_book)",
      "options": ["{'Cortez': '555-1234'}", "Cortez: 555-1234", "555-1234", "Cortez"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q14",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "phone_book = {\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\", \"Lance\": \"555-5678\"}\nprint(phone_book[0])",
      "options": [
        "It prints 555-1234, the first number",
        "It stops with a KeyError: 0 is not one of its keys",
        "It prints Cortez",
        "It prints nothing"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q15",
      "text": "In the Crew Database mission, which line adds the key \"station\"?",
      "options": [
        "crew.append(station)",
        "station = crew[\"station\"]",
        "crew[\"station\"] = station",
        "crew = {\"station\": station}"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q16",
      "text": "In the Crew Database mission, which line adds 1 to the age inside crew?",
      "options": [
        "age = age + 1",
        "crew[\"age\"] = 1",
        "crew[\"age\" + 1]",
        "crew[\"age\"] = crew[\"age\"] + 1"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q17",
      "text": "In the Crew Database mission, which line decides to print Rank: unknown?",
      "options": [
        "if \"rank\" not in crew:",
        "if crew[\"rank\"] == \"unknown\":",
        "if \"rank\" in crew:",
        "if crew == \"rank\":"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q18",
      "text": "In the mission, `crew = {\"name\": name}`. What is the difference between `\"name\"` and `name`?",
      "options": [
        "None, both are the same text",
        "\"name\" is the key, a text; name is the variable that holds the value, like Tommy",
        "name is the key and \"name\" is the value",
        "The quotes make the key hidden"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q19",
      "text": "What goes between a key and its value?",
      "options": ["=", ",", ":", ";"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q20",
      "text": "What goes between two key: value pairs?",
      "options": ["A colon", "A semicolon", "The word and", "A comma"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q21",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "player = {\"name\": \"Tommy\", \"weapons\": [\"bat\", \"pistol\", \"shotgun\"]}\nprint(player[\"weapons\"][1])",
      "options": ["pistol", "bat", "['bat', 'pistol', 'shotgun']", "It stops with an error"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q22",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "phone_book = {\"Cortez\": \"555-1234\", \"Lance\": \"555-5678\"}\ndel phone_book[\"Lance\"]\nprint(phone_book[\"Lance\"])",
      "options": [
        "It prints 555-5678",
        "It stops with a KeyError: del removed the key Lance",
        "It prints an empty line",
        "It prints None"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q23",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "ages = {\"Tommy\": 42}\nprint(\"tommy\" in ages)",
      "options": [
        "True: in doesn't care about upper or lower case",
        "Tommy",
        "False: tommy and Tommy are different keys",
        "It stops with an error"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q24",
      "text": "Which of these is an empty dictionary?",
      "options": ["[]", "{:}", "()", "{}"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q25",
      "text": "phone_book holds Cortez and Lance. After `phone_book[\"Sonny\"] = \"555-0001\"` and `del phone_book[\"Lance\"]`, how many key: value pairs does it hold?",
      "options": ["2", "3", "1", "4"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q26",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "ship = {\"fuel\": 50}\nship[\"fuel\"] = ship[\"fuel\"] - 20\nprint(ship[\"fuel\"])",
      "options": ["50", "30", "20", "It stops with an error: fuel is already there"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q27",
      "text": "When does the code under `if \"rank\" not in crew:` run?",
      "options": [
        "When crew[\"rank\"] is empty",
        "Never: not in only works on lists",
        "When crew has no key \"rank\"",
        "When crew has the key \"rank\""
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q28",
      "text": "What does `phone_book[\"Lance\"]` give back?",
      "options": [
        "The key Lance",
        "Lance's position in phone_book",
        "True or False, whether Lance is in phone_book",
        "The value stored under the key Lance"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q29",
      "text": "Is `{\"Tommy\": 90, \"Lance\": 90}` a valid dictionary?",
      "options": [
        "Yes: keys have to differ, but values may repeat",
        "No: two values can't be the same",
        "Yes, but print() shows only one of them",
        "No: the values have to be text"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q30",
      "text": "Which line reads Phil's number from phone_book?",
      "options": [
        "phone_book(\"Phil\")",
        "phone_book[\"Phil\"]",
        "phone_book[Phil]",
        "phone_book.Phil"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    }
  ],
